6904056	Judging from the parallel passage in KUB 5.4+ rev. III 6, the space was probably left blank.
6904057	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;The restoration of this and the following lines is based on similar passages in the same text (see, e.g. obv. I 16 ff. and obv. I 26ff.).&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6904058	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;According to the photo, the sign is written with an additional Winkelhaken and a second horizontal wedge. Probably the scribe initially wanted to write the sign &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;RU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; and thus the 3. pers. pl. imperative &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;taruppantaru&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; as in obv. II 10 and obv. I 47. &lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6904059	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Text: &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;PA&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; instead of &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;RU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6904060	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;End of this and the following lines restored from the analogous passages i 1ff.; 16ff. etc.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6904061	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;In contrast to cuneiform copy by Walther in KUB 5.4, the vertical is completely visible on the photo.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6904062	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;The broken end of the line was probably blank since attributes that accompany the word &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;MUŠEN&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;ḪI.A&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt; &quot;birds&quot;, such as &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ḫatuga/i-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &quot;terrible, scary&quot; or &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;laḫlaḫ(ḫ)ima-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &quot;concern, worry, agitation&quot;, usually precede it. For references see &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;HW2 III/1&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, 526-527 s.v. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ḫatuga/i-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; and CHD L-N, p. 11-12 s.v. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;laḫlaḫ(ḫ)ima-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6904063	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Text: &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;TI&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6904064	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Restoration based on obv. I 3 (partly broken); obv. I 18; obv. I 28; obv. II 9; rev. III 5. Alternatively, the less frequent spelling &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;me-ia-an-na-aš-ša-aš-ši&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; could be restored (cf. obv. I 39; obv. II 22).&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
